 "text": "Hi, how you going? Then why not try something like The History of Britain, which gives five thousand years of background up today? Definitely start there, it's where it all begins. Then move on from there, each episode is few hours long and there are multiple series. Not at all, it' gripping stuff. You can start with the Roman ones and skip the bits about small wars in the Middle East. How about the story of the world in ten miles and ten minutes, it's perfect for short bursts. You' enjoy the long one when you want sink into detail, and the ten minute one when you only have five minutes. History at its best.",
